# KAMCH ERP — USER MANAGEMENT MODULE
## Final Implementation Specification

### 1. Objective

Implement the User Management module for Krishna Ayurvedic Medical College and Hospital (KAMCH ERP).

This module must provide secure account creation, role assignment, account suspension and deactivation, password management, session security, and role-based visibility throughout the ERP.

The requirements in this document are authoritative.

The Fees Management module has already been implemented and fixed. Preserve it and all other working features.

**Implement only the User Management requirements below. Do not conduct a separate audit, rebuild the ERP, or add unrelated features.**

---

## 2. Mandatory Development Rules

1. Work within the existing project and technology stack.
2. Reuse the existing database connection, authentication system, session management, password hashing, CSRF protection, logging, and UI components wherever they are correct.
3. Make the smallest safe changes necessary to implement the requirements.
4. Do not redesign or rebuild unrelated modules.
5. Do not delete, reset, or recreate the database.
6. Do not remove or overwrite existing users or their records.
7. Use safe, additive database migrations when required.
8. Do not introduce a second authentication system or duplicate role system.
9. Do not create demo users or fake student, teacher, department, or account records.
10. Do not hardcode account lists, user data, permissions, or department names into the frontend. Store and retrieve applicable data through the database and existing authorization mechanisms.
11. Enforce authorization on the server/API. Hiding a menu item alone is not security.
12. Do not create additional roles without explicit approval.
13. Do not add student login or faculty login functionality in this phase.
14. Complete implementation, test it, fix introduced errors, and provide a concise completion report.
15. Do not begin another module after finishing this one.

