## 5. Account Creation

Only the following roles can create user accounts:
- Super Admin.
- Principal.
- Secretary.

Account creation must be performed through the existing User Management interface.

The account creator must be able to:
- Enter the person's full name.
- Set a unique username.
- Enter an email address where applicable.
- Select an allowed role.
- Associate a department account with its department.
- Set an initial temporary password.
- Activate the account.

Do not invent unnecessary mandatory fields.

Validate required fields on both frontend and backend.

Prevent duplicate usernames. Validate email uniqueness when email is supplied and used as a login identifier.

The account creator manually sets the initial temporary password.

There is no separate approval process. Once created and activated by an authorized creator, the account can log in, subject to the mandatory first-login password change.

### Role assignment restrictions

- Super Admin may create all supported account types.
- Principal and Secretary may create and manage permitted accounts but cannot create, modify, suspend, deactivate, or change the role of the Super Admin account.
- No role may create another Super Admin account unless explicitly authorized by the existing system's protected Super Admin provisioning process.
- Office, Library, and Department accounts cannot create login accounts.

Do not create student or faculty login accounts in this phase.

