## 12. Department Management Integration

The User Management module must support the department account structure.

Super Admin must be able to:
- Create a department record.
- Edit department details.
- Assign one department account to that department.
- Activate, suspend, reactivate, or deactivate its department account.
- Reset its account password.
- Review its account status.

A department account must have a reliable database relationship to exactly one department.

Prevent an account from being associated with multiple departments unless the existing schema explicitly supports and the specification later authorizes that arrangement.

Department isolation must be enforced on the server for every department-specific endpoint.

A department must not be able to:
- View another department's records.
- Upload marks for another department.
- Change its own department association.
- Access User Management.
- Change its role.
- Access college-wide fee or library administration.

Do not build a separate marks-management system as part of this module. Provide only the necessary account and department integration.

