## 14. Audit Logging

Use the existing audit logging service.

Record meaningful account-management actions, including:
- Account creation.
- Role assignment and role changes.
- Account activation and deactivation.
- Suspension and reactivation.
- Password resets.
- Successful and failed login attempts where appropriate.
- Temporary lockout events.
- Session invalidation.
- Department creation and assignment.
- Unauthorized access attempts where appropriate.

Each relevant event should identify:
- Acting user, when available.
- Affected account or record.
- Action performed.
- Timestamp.
- Before/after values for changes where appropriate.
- Reason where applicable.

Never log:
- Plain-text passwords.
- Password hashes.
- Session tokens.
- CSRF tokens.
- Other sensitive authentication secrets.

Preserve historical audit entries even when an account is deactivated.

Use the existing audit retention policy, with a minimum retention period of one year if the existing implementation supports the established project requirement.

