## 18. Required Testing

Test actual functionality, not just page rendering.

### Account creation
- Super Admin creates an account.
- Principal creates an allowed account.
- Secretary creates an allowed account.
- Duplicate usernames are rejected.
- Duplicate email identifiers are rejected where applicable.
- Office, Library, and Department accounts cannot create accounts.
- Student and Faculty login accounts cannot be created through this workflow.

### Password security
- Temporary password works for first login.
- First login requires a password change.
- Protected APIs cannot be accessed before the required password change.
- Password reset invalidates active sessions.
- Reset users must change the new temporary password.
- Passwords are not stored or logged in plain text.

### Roles and visibility
- Super Admin sees every account and module.
- Principal sees permitted accounts and modules but cannot see or manipulate Super Admin.
- Secretary sees permitted accounts and modules but cannot see or manipulate Super Admin.
- Office members cannot see User Management.
- Library users see only Library functionality.
- Department accounts see only their own department's permitted functionality.
- Teacher records do not create login accounts.
- Students do not receive login accounts.
- Unauthorized navigation items and buttons are absent.

### Server-side security
- Direct unauthorized API requests are rejected.
- Principal and Secretary cannot access the Super Admin account by guessing an ID.
- Department accounts cannot access another department by changing request parameters.
- Users cannot elevate their own roles.
- Suspended and deactivated accounts cannot authenticate.
- Previous sessions stop working after a new login.
- Session invalidation works after suspension and deactivation.

### Failed login handling
- Five failed attempts do not trigger the sixth-attempt threshold prematurely.
- Six consecutive failures trigger the 30-minute lockout.
- Correct credentials do not bypass an active lockout.
- Login becomes possible after the lockout expires, assuming the account is otherwise valid.

### Regression
- Existing login functionality continues working.
- Fees Management remains functional.
- Student and teacher records remain intact.
- Existing payments, receipts, audit logs, and database relationships remain intact.
- Existing build and type checks pass.

Run the available type check, production build, and relevant automated tests. Report only tests that were actually executed.

